description:
Implements: docs/PROTOCOL.md §1–§10 as written by vtt-5su.2; DESIGN.md §5.2, §7.

Create `packages/protocol` (`@vtt/protocol`), scaffolded per CLAUDE.md: exports `"."` → `./src/index.ts`, `tsconfig.json` extending the base, `typecheck` script, `vitest.config.ts` with `test.name: "@vtt/protocol"`; dependencies `@vtt/schema` (workspace) and `zod` 4.6.7; also add `"@vtt/protocol": "workspace:*"` and `"zod": "4.6.7"` to `@vtt/authority`'s dependencies (so later authority beads need not edit them); lockfile rides along. Exclusive files: everything in `packages/protocol/src` except `client.ts` and `mirror.ts` (vtt-5su.7), and `test/schema-*.test.ts`. Package index rule (CLAUDE.md): one sorted `export * from "./<module>"` line per module.

Modules: `version.ts` (`PROTOCOL_VERSION = 1`, `DEFAULT_PORT = 4747`, `LIMITS`), `values.ts`, `views.ts`, `ops.ts` (`WireOp`, `WIRE_OP_TYPES`), `methods.ts` (per-method params/result types and schemas, `METHODS` table with name, params schema, result schema, kind `write | query | explain | subscribe`, and `Params<M>`/`Result<M>`), `messages.ts` (`ClientMessage`, `ServerMessage`, `ProtocolError`, `ProtocolRejection`, `CommitEvent`, `SubscriptionDelta`, `SaveEvent`, `CLOSE_CODES`, `ProtocolFailure`, `parseClientMessage`, `parseServerMessage`).

All schemas are zod, strict objects (unknown keys rejected; `__proto__` rejected as a key anywhere, as FIXTURES §1), discriminated on `type` (requests on `method`). Values reuse `@vtt/schema`'s value, error value (vtt-o9i.2), shape, viewers, `ActionDef`, `Actor`, `Effect`, `OpGroup`, `Rejection`, `Snapshot`, `Board` schemas unchanged (vtt-75c.3, vtt-75c.4).

Types (exact field names):

```ts
type Viewer = { type: "gm" } | { type: "character"; id: ObjectId };
type RedactedValue = { type: "redacted" };
type WireValue = Value | ErrorValue | RedactedValue;   // redacted may also appear inside lists and viewers values
type BindingName = string;                             // "$" followed by id characters
type CellView = { value: WireValue; kind: "literal" | "formula" | "structural";
                  source?: string; overridden?: boolean; visibility?: ViewersValue };
type ActionView = { name: string; when?: string; steps?: string[] };
type ObjectView = { id: ObjectId; is_template: boolean; is_character: boolean;
                    cells: Record<string, CellView>; actions: ActionView[] };
type BoardView = { id: BoardId; name?: string };
type Cover = { key: string; board: BoardId;
               region: { position: [number, number]; rotation: number; shape: Shape } | { whole_board: true } };
type GroupHeader = { index: number; revision: number; actor: Actor; kind: "edit" | "action" | "undo"; label: string };
type GroupView = GroupHeader & { base_revision: number; origin?: { object: ObjectId; action: string };
                 undoes?: number; undone: boolean; names: Record<ObjectId, string>; effects?: Effect[] };
type ObjRef = ObjectId | BindingName;
type Destination = { type: "board"; board: BoardId; position: [number, number] }
                 | { type: "container"; container: ObjRef; index?: number };
type ObjectInit = { is_template?: boolean; is_zone?: boolean; is_character?: boolean; tag?: string[]; shape?: Shape;
                    cells?: Record<string, CellContent>; cell_visibility?: Record<string, ViewersValue>; actions?: ActionDef[] };
```

`WireOp`, 19 kinds (`{type, …}`; object fields are `ObjRef`): `set_value {object, cell, value}`, `set_formula {object, cell, source}`, `clear_override {object, cell}`, `delete_cell {object, cell}`, `rename_cell {object, from, to}`, `set_cell_visibility {object, cell, viewers: ViewersValue | null}`, `set_tag {object, tags: string[]}`, `set_shape {object, shape: Shape | null}`, `set_template_flag {object, value: boolean}`, `set_character_flag {object, value: boolean}`, `set_actions {object, actions: ActionDef[]}`, `reorder {container, permutation: number[]}`, `add_board {id, name?}`, `rename_board {id, name}`, `remove_board {id}`, `create_object {id?, as?: BindingName, to: Destination, init?: ObjectInit}`, `spawn {template, to: Destination, cells?: Record<string, CellContent>, as?: BindingName, owned?: Record<ObjectId, BindingName>}`, `move {object, to: Destination}`, `remove {object}`. Inside op values (set_value, init cells, spawn cells, viewers) a ref's `object` may be a `BindingName`; in views and results never.

Messages:

```ts
// client → server
{ type: "hello"; protocol: 1; token: string; client: { name: string; kind: "ui" | "agent" | "test" }; agent_name?: string }
{ type: "request"; id: string /* 1–64 chars */; method: M; params: Params<M> }
// server → client
{ type: "welcome"; protocol: 1; session: string; actor: Actor; revision: number; boards: BoardView[];
  table: { name: string; path: string | null }; limits: Limits }
{ type: "response"; id: string; ok: true; result: Result<M> }
{ type: "response"; id: string | null; ok: false; error: ProtocolError }       // id null when unparseable
{ type: "event"; event: "commit"; revision: number; group: GroupHeader; boards?: BoardView[]; deltas: SubscriptionDelta[] }
{ type: "event"; event: "save"; status: "saved" | "saved_not_durable" | "failed"; revision: number; message?: string }
{ type: "goodbye"; reason: string }
type SubscriptionDelta = { subscription: string; objects: ObjectView[]; removed: ObjectId[];
                           covers?: { upsert: Cover[]; removed: string[] }; groups?: GroupView[] };
type ProtocolError = { code: ProtocolErrorCode; message: string; details?: unknown };
type ProtocolErrorCode = "bad_request" | "unknown_method" | "unauthorized" | "protocol_version" | "busy"
  | "too_large" | "not_found" | "unsupported" | "internal" | "disconnected" | "timeout";
type ProtocolRejection = Rejection
  | { type: "stale_write"; base_revision: number; revision: number; truncated: boolean;
      conflicts: { index: number; revision: number; actor: Actor; label: string; keys: string[] }[] }
  | { type: "undo_target_changed"; expected: number; actual: number | null };
```

Methods (17; `viewer` defaults to `{type:"gm"}`):

| Method | Params | Result |
|---|---|---|
| transact | base_revision, ops: WireOp[] (1..max_ops), label? (≤200), txn_id?, actor? | `{status:"committed", revision, index, created: {op_index, id}[], copies: {op_index, root, copies: Record<ObjectId,ObjectId>}[], bindings: Record<BindingName, ObjectId>}` or `{status:"rejected", rejection: ProtocolRejection, op_index?}` |
| undo | target: {type:"latest"} \| {type:"mine"} \| {type:"actor", actor} \| {type:"group", index}; expect_index?; label? | same shapes; created, copies, bindings empty |
| invoke | object, action, base_revision | always error `unsupported` until M5 |
| save | {} | `{status, revision, message?}` |
| list_objects | viewer?, filter?: {board?, container?, tag?, name?, is_template?, is_zone?, is_character?}, cells?: "all" \| "structural" \| string[] (default "structural"), cursor?, limit? (default 50, ≤ max_page) | `{revision, objects, next_cursor: string \| null}` |
| get_objects | ids (1..max_ids), viewer?, cells? (default "all") | `{revision, objects, missing: ObjectId[]}` |
| evaluate | source (≤ max_source_length), this? | `{revision, value: WireValue}` |
| zones | board, viewer? | `{revision, zones: {id, contents: ObjectId[], view: ObjectView}[]}` |
| at_position | board, position: [x, y], viewer? | `{revision, objects: ObjectId[], zones: ObjectId[]}` |
| changes_since | revision, viewer?, limit? (default 100, ≤ max_groups) | `{revision, groups: GroupView[], truncated, more}` |
| log | before?, limit? (default 50, ≤ max_page), viewer?, effects?: boolean | `{first_index, next_index, undo_barrier, groups: GroupView[]}` newest first |
| document | {} | `{snapshot: Snapshot, log: {first_index, groups: OpGroup[], undo_barrier}}` |
| explain_cell | object, cell, viewer?, depth? (1..max_explain_depth, default 1) | ExplainCellResult |
| explain_group | index, viewer? | ExplainGroupResult |
| explain_action | object, action, viewer? | ExplainActionResult |
| subscribe | scope: {type:"board", board} \| {type:"objects", ids, subtree?} \| {type:"all"} \| {type:"log"}; viewer?; cells?: "all" \| "structural" (default "all") | `{subscription, revision, objects, covers: Cover[], groups?: GroupView[]}` |
| unsubscribe | subscription | `{}` |

Explain result types (PROTOCOL.md §9):

```ts
type DepNode = { type: "cell"; object: ObjectId | null; cell: string; value?: WireValue; hidden?: true; dependencies?: DepNode[] }
             | { type: "exists"; object: ObjectId | null; exists?: boolean } | { type: "index" };
type ExplainCellResult = { revision: number; object: ObjectId; cell: string; view: CellView;
  content: { type: "literal" } | { type: "structural" } | { type: "formula"; source?: string; overridden: boolean; parses: boolean; syntax_error?: string };
  dependencies: DepNode[]; truncated: boolean;
  error_chain?: { object: ObjectId | null; cell: string | null; code: string }[];
  last_write?: GroupHeader & { cause: "edit" | "roll" } };
type ExplainGroupResult = { group: GroupView; action?: { object: ObjectId; name: string; when?: string; steps: string[]; current: true } };
type ExplainActionResult = { object: ObjectId; action: string;
  when?: { source?: string; value: WireValue; enabled: boolean; reason?: "when_false" | "when_error" }; steps?: string[] };
```

`Limits` = `{max_message_bytes: 1048576, max_ops: 1000, max_page: 200, max_ids: 200, max_subscriptions: 16, max_explain_depth: 4, max_explain_nodes: 200, max_source_length: 10000, max_groups: 500, max_requests_per_second: 200, max_buffered_bytes: 8388608}` (PROTOCOL.md §10). `CLOSE_CODES = {protocol: 4400, unauthorized: 4401, hello_timeout: 4408, slow_consumer: 4429, shutdown: 1001}`. `class ProtocolFailure extends Error { error: ProtocolError }`, constructed as `new ProtocolFailure(code, message, details?)`, is thrown by authority handlers and turned into error responses by the router. `parseClientMessage(text)` / `parseServerMessage(text)` return `{ok: true, message} | {ok: false, error: ProtocolError}` and never throw.

Done when: `test/schema-messages.test.ts` round-trips (parse → deep-equal) a hand-written example of every client and server message, every method's params and result, every one of the 19 `WireOp` kinds, every `ProtocolRejection` and every error code; it rejects an unknown key at the message, params, op and view levels, a `__proto__` key in `cells`, a request with an unknown method, a `$name` ref inside a view's value, a `transact` with zero ops and with `max_ops + 1` ops, and a `list_objects` with `limit` above `max_page`; `parseClientMessage` returns an error (not a throw) for invalid JSON; `METHODS` has exactly the 17 methods and `WIRE_OP_TYPES` exactly the 19 ops; a type-level test (`expectTypeOf`) checks `Result<"transact">` and `Params<"subscribe">`; `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm format:check`, `pnpm test` exit 0.

Out of scope: the client and mirror (vtt-5su.7); any server code; MCP (vtt-5su.11); `invoke` behaviour and face-layout fields (M5).

Depends on: vtt-5su.2, vtt-75c.3, vtt-75c.4.

Implements: DESIGN.md §7 (operation records with resolved effects, groups, undo as an operation, identity effects, file contents), §4.1 (identity reservation), §4.4 (per-cell visibility metadata), as written by vtt-75c.2; FIXTURES.md §6 (rejection reasons), §7 (log effects), §8.

Add packages/schema/src/ops.ts and src/file.ts to @vtt/schema with zod schemas. Package index rule: add only this bead's export lines to src/index.ts; Biome requires the lines sorted, so place yours in order; never edit others'. Import specifiers have no .ts suffix. Values inside effects are the schema value types unchanged (vtt-o9i.2).

```ts
type Actor = { type: "gm" } | { type: "character"; id: ObjectId } | { type: "agent"; name?: string };
type Location = { type: "board"; board: BoardId } | { type: "container"; container: ObjectId; index: number };
type CellState = Cell | null;  // null = absent
type Effect =
  | { type: "cell"; object; cell; before: CellState; after: CellState; cause: "edit" | "roll" }
  | { type: "cell_visibility"; object; cell; before: ViewersValue | null; after: ViewersValue | null }
  | { type: "field"; object; field: "tag" | "shape" | "is_template" | "is_character"; before; after }
  | { type: "place"; object; before: Location; after: Location }
  | { type: "create"; objects: TableObject[]; location: Location }   // subtree, preorder, root first
  | { type: "remove"; objects: TableObject[]; location: Location }   // same shape; inverse of create
  | { type: "reorder"; container; before: ObjectId[]; after: ObjectId[] }
  | { type: "board"; before: Board | null; after: Board | null }
  | { type: "allocate"; ids: ObjectId[]; seq_before: number; seq_after: number } // ids reserved by this group
  | { type: "retire"; ids: ObjectId[] };                                          // ids newly added to retired_ids
type OpGroup = {
  index: number;                         // absolute, stable across compaction
  base_revision: number; revision: number; actor: Actor;
  kind: "edit" | "action" | "undo"; label: string;
  origin?: { object: ObjectId; action: string };
  undoes?: number;                       // absolute index, for kind "undo"
  names: Record<ObjectId, string>;       // name of every touched object at commit time (removed: just before removal)
  effects: Effect[];
};
type Rejection =
  | { type: "protected_cell"; object; cell }
  | { type: "containment_cycle"; object; container }
  | { type: "undo_conflict"; target: number; conflicting: number[]; message: string }
  | { type: "nothing_to_undo" }
  | { type: "type_error"; object; cell; expected: string }
  | { type: "invalid"; message: string };   // unknown object, bad index, retired id, etc.
type TableFile = {
  format: "a-table-of-dumb-objects"; schema_version: number;
  snapshot: Snapshot; snapshot_hash: string;   // "sha256:<hex>" of canonical snapshot JSON
  log: { first_index: number; groups: OpGroup[]; undo_barrier: number };
  assets: string[];                            // paths relative to the file's directory
};
```

A `cell` effect's `after` is the resolved state: for an `add` the sum, for an override the override, for a roll the roll result with `cause: "roll"`. `place` covers board-to-board, board-to-container, container-to-board and within-container moves; the accompanying `position`, `rotation`, `z` changes are separate `cell` effects in the same group. `allocate` records ids reserved by spawn, object creation (generated or explicit) or board creation, and the `next_seq` change; `retire` records exactly the ids it newly adds to `retired_ids` (by object or board removal, or by undoing a creation), never ids already retired, so a rewind can remove exactly those. User undo never reverses `allocate` or `retire` (identity is reserved for the document's lifetime). Only historical rewind reverses them, through an internal historical-inverse representation owned by vtt-75c.5; that representation is never persisted and is not an `Effect` (the persisted effects are only those listed here). `SCHEMA_VERSION = 1`, `FILE_FORMAT = "a-table-of-dumb-objects"`. `log.groups` holds retained groups with indices `first_index …`; `undo_barrier` is an absolute index.

Done when: schemas round-trip a hand-written example of every effect kind (including `cell_visibility`, `allocate`, `retire`) and every rejection kind (parse then deep-equal); unknown keys are rejected; `TableFileSchema` rejects a missing `schema_version` and a `format` other than the constant; an exported `toFixtureReason(rejection)` maps `Rejection` to the FIXTURES §6 reasons (`protected_cell`, `containment_cycle`, `undo_conflict`, `nothing_to_undo`; `type_error` maps to `step_error` #TYPE for M5) and a test documents the mapping; `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm format:check`, `pnpm test` exit 0.

Out of scope: docs (vtt-75c.2); applying or inverting effects (vtt-75c.5); migration logic and file I/O (vtt-75c.11); action-level rejections `when_false`, `when_error`, `step_error` beyond the `type_error` mapping (M5).

Depends on: vtt-75c.3.
